Subject: [PATCH 1/4] subscription: per-subscription non-blocking event ordering

dispatchEvent spawns a new goroutine for every event. The goroutines race
to send on sub.Events, so events arrive in random order. This is observable
under -cpu=2 or higher with bursts of 256+ events.

Replace the per-event goroutine design with a per-subscription ordered queue:

- New subscriptionInbox: a mutex-guarded FIFO slice with a 1-buffered signal
  channel. push() appends without blocking the caller and sends a non-blocking
  wake signal. The read loop (handleMessage on the main-loop goroutine) is
  never blocked, so it can still deliver OK, EOSE, CLOSED, AUTH and NOTICE
  for every subscription and publish on the connection. A consumer that
  publishes to the same relay and waits for OK inside an event handler (the
  OK arrives on the same read loop) no longer deadlocks.

- Overflow: when the queue exceeds subscriptionInboxCap (4096), the inbox is
  marked closed and the subscription is closed via handleClosed with an
  overflow reason. No events are silently dropped — the consumer knows the
  subscription ended and can resubscribe from its cursor.

- Dispatcher goroutine: waits on the signal channel, drains the queue, and
  delivers items to Events in FIFO order under mu.RLock. On Context.Done,
  it releases storedwg for remaining items and exits.

- Subscriptions without PrepareSubscription (test helpers) have a nil inbox
  and fall back to the legacy per-goroutine path.

- Teardown: sets channelsClosed, calls inbox.close(), waits for the dispatcher,
  then closes Events and countResult.

Also includes:
- closedHandled atomic.Bool guard on handleClosed to prevent a second CLOSED
  from leaking a goroutine.
- isCount field on SubscriptionOptions so countResult is created before the
  subscription is stored in the map (fixing a race where a COUNT reply arrives
  before countInternal sets countResult).

Tests: subscription_order_test.go
- TestDispatchEventPreservesOrderLive (1024 live events, wire order)
- TestDispatchEventPreservesOrderStored (256 stored, EOSE after last)
- TestDispatchEventOrderAcrossStoredAndLive (stored + live, each in order)
- TestDispatchEventNonBlockingUnblocksOnCancel (1000 events without reader)
- TestInboxDoesNotBlockOtherSubscriptions (sub A blocked, sub B unaffected)
- TestPublishFromEventHandlerDoesNotDeadlock (publish+OK from handler)
- TestInboxOverflowClosesSubscription (overflow closes with reason)

Run with: go test -cpu=1,2,8 -count=20 -run 'TestDispatchEvent|TestInbox|TestPublishFrom'
